    <exercises xml:id="exercises-loci-inequalities">
        <exercise xml:id="ex-shade-a-lens">
            <statement><p><m>AB = 4\,\text{cm}</m>. Show the region where <m>PA \lt 3\,\text{cm}</m> and <m>PB \lt 3\,\text{cm}</m> by shading the unwanted parts. Describe its boundary.</p></statement>
            <answer><p>The overlap of the two discs, bounded by two dashed arcs that meet at two points.</p></answer>
            <solution><p>Draw circles of radius <m>3\,\text{cm}</m> about <m>A</m> and about <m>B</m>, both dashed. Shade outside each circle. The region left clear, inside both, is a lens shape. Its corners are on the perpendicular bisector of <m>AB</m>, <m>2\,\text{cm}</m> from <m>A</m> along <m>AB</m> and <m>\sqrt{3^2 - 2^2} \approx 2.2\,\text{cm}</m> either side of <m>AB</m>.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-grid-region-test">
            <statement><p>A region is the set of points less than <m>5</m> units from <m>A(0, 0)</m> and nearer to <m>B(6, 0)</m> than to <m>A</m>. Test the points <m>(4, 2)</m>, <m>(2, 1)</m> and <m>(4, 4)</m>.</p></statement>
            <answer><p><m>(4, 2)</m> is in the region; <m>(2, 1)</m> is not (nearer to <m>A</m>); <m>(4, 4)</m> is not (about <m>5.66</m> units from <m>A</m>).</p></answer>
            <solution><p>The perpendicular bisector of <m>AB</m> is <m>x = 3</m>, so <q>nearer to <m>B</m></q> means <m>x \gt 3</m>. <m>(4, 2)</m>: <m>4^2 + 2^2 = 20 \lt 25</m> and <m>x = 4 \gt 3</m>: in. <m>(2, 1)</m>: <m>x = 2 \lt 3</m>: out. <m>(4, 4)</m>: <m>16 + 16 = 32 \gt 25</m>: out.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-write-the-inequalities">
            <statement><p>Write as inequalities: the points less than <m>2\,\text{m}</m> from the straight path <m>l</m> and more than <m>5\,\text{m}</m> from the tree <m>T</m>.</p></statement>
            <answer><p>(distance of <m>P</m> from <m>l</m>) <m>\lt 2\,\text{m}</m> and <m>PT \gt 5\,\text{m}</m>.</p></answer>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-dispensary-site">
            <statement><p>A dispensary in Garissa County must be within <m>6\,\text{km}</m> of village <m>A</m>, at least <m>2\,\text{km}</m> from the straight main road and nearer to <m>A</m> than to village <m>B</m>, which is <m>8\,\text{km}</m> from <m>A</m> along the road. Using <m>1\,\text{cm}</m> to represent <m>1\,\text{km}</m>, construct the region where the dispensary can go, shading the unwanted parts.</p></statement>
            <answer><p>Inside the circle of radius <m>6\,\text{cm}</m> about <m>A</m> (solid), outside the strip of width <m>2\,\text{cm}</m> on each side of the road (solid lines), and on <m>A</m>'s side of the perpendicular bisector of <m>AB</m> (dashed).</p></answer>
            <solution><p><q>Within <m>6\,\text{km}</m></q> includes <m>6\,\text{km}</m>, so the circle is solid. <q>At least <m>2\,\text{km}</m></q> includes <m>2\,\text{km}</m>, so the two lines parallel to the road, <m>2\,\text{cm}</m> from it, are solid and the region is outside the strip. <q>Nearer to <m>A</m></q> excludes the bisector, which is <m>4\,\text{cm}</m> from <m>A</m> and is dashed. Shade outside the circle, inside the strip and on <m>B</m>'s side of the bisector. The clear region is two pieces, one on each side of the road.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-offside-positions">
            <statement><p>The second-last defender is <m>8\,\text{m}</m> from the goal line and the ball is <m>15\,\text{m}</m> from it. Attackers stand <m>6\,\text{m}</m>, <m>8\,\text{m}</m> and <m>9\,\text{m}</m> from the goal line, in the opponents' half. Which are in an offside position?</p></statement>
            <answer><p>Only the attacker <m>6\,\text{m}</m> from the goal line.</p></answer>
            <solution><p>The defender is nearer the goal line than the ball, so the offside region is the strip less than <m>8\,\text{m}</m> from the goal line. The attacker at <m>8\,\text{m}</m> is level (not offside) and the one at <m>9\,\text{m}</m> is outside the strip.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise xml:id="ex-sixty-degree-region">
            <title>Challenge: A Sixty-Degree Region</title>
            <statement><p><m>AB = 6\,\text{cm}</m>. Describe the region on one side of <m>AB</m> where angle <m>APB \ge 60^{\circ}</m>. Is the point <m>5\,\text{cm}</m> in front of the midpoint <m>M</m> of <m>AB</m> in it?</p></statement>
            <hint><p>Find the centre and radius of the arc on which angle <m>APB = 60^{\circ}</m>, then how far in front of <m>M</m> the arc reaches.</p></hint>
            <answer><p>The region between <m>AB</m> and the arc of radius <m>3.46\,\text{cm}</m>, arc included (solid). The arc is <m>5.20\,\text{cm}</m> in front of <m>M</m>, so the point is in the region (angle about <m>61.9^{\circ}</m>).</p></answer>
            <solution><p>The arc has radius <m>\dfrac{6}{2\sin 60^{\circ}} \approx 3.46\,\text{cm}</m> and its centre <m>O</m> is on the perpendicular bisector, <m>OM = \dfrac{3}{\tan 60^{\circ}} \approx 1.73\,\text{cm}</m> from <m>M</m>. So the arc reaches <m>1.73 + 3.46 \approx 5.20\,\text{cm}</m> in front of <m>M</m>. Points inside the arc see <m>AB</m> at more than <m>60^{\circ}</m>, and <m>\ge</m> includes the arc. The point <m>5\,\text{cm}</m> in front of <m>M</m> is inside: angle <m>2\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{5}\right) \approx 61.9^{\circ}</m>.</p></solution>
        </exercise>
    </exercises>

    <axiom component="lesson-plan">
        <title>Differentiation</title>
        <table xml:id="table-differentiation-loci-inequalities">
            <title>Differentiation Strategies</title>
            <tabular halign="left" top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                <row header="yes" bottom="medium"><cell>Learner Group</cell><cell>Strategy and Learning Experience</cell></row>
                <row><cell>Struggling Learners (Support)</cell><cell>Take one condition at a time: shade its unwanted side, test a point in the clear region, then add the next condition. Work <xref ref="example-describing-a-region"/> and <xref ref="example-offside-line"/>. Assign <xref ref="ex-grid-region-test"/> and <xref ref="ex-offside-positions"/>.</cell></row>
                <row><cell>On-Level Learners (Core)</cell><cell>Full activity and all examples. Assign <xref ref="ex-shade-a-lens"/> to <xref ref="ex-offside-positions"/>.</cell></row>
                <row><cell>Advanced Learners (Challenge)</cell><cell>All exercises including <xref ref="ex-sixty-degree-region"/>. Extension: show, by shading the unwanted parts, the region less than <m>2\,\text{m}</m> from a straight wall <m>6\,\text{m}</m> long and more than <m>1\,\text{m}</m> from both of its ends. (Answer: the stadium shape round the wall, two <m>6\,\text{m}</m> sides joined by semicircles of radius <m>2\,\text{m}</m>, all dashed, with two dashed circles of radius <m>1\,\text{m}</m> about the ends of the wall removed.)</cell></row>
            </tabular>
        </table>
    </axiom>

